silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_02_yoneda_lemma_statement_concrete_anchor silm:hasExample "In 'YonedaLemmaStatementConcreteAnchor', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, D_Mittens_Category: the locally small category used as the instantiation of C in the Yoneda lemma statement; objects = twelve source nodes + MittensColimitApex; morphisms = the twelve typed legs plus identity arrows and compositions; also, MittensColimitApex: the concrete instantiation of the object A in the Yoneda lemma; the colimit of D_Mittens; Mittens-the-individual-cat assembled from all twelve legs; also, ClinicalLabelPresheaf: the concrete instantiation of the presheaf F; assigns to each D_Mittens source node X the set of clinical labels for X stored in VetRecord_77 or associated clinic systems." .
